{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794547867188,"sessionID":"ses_e2c9ec714ffefg1SEdXaW10eW8","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3635807002d3pKUKp5H7NHWa","sessionID":"ses_e2c9ec714ffefg1SEdXaW10eW8","messageID":"msg_1d36352520014LKUOgIEKJDQMk","type":"tool","id":"call_72a2519fa15c45c6a55ef951","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":8,"offset":79,"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md, lines 79-86\n79: \n80: A line whose locator names no checkout keeps null offer fields and `offerError` `no_checkout`, and the rest of the log is still written with `offerBackfilled: true`.\n81: \n82: `--brief-only` keeps every offer field exactly as the input line holds it, present or absent, and recomputes only `briefDelivered`, because a recorded offer belongs to the head the turn saw and replaying it would describe a different head. Brief delivery now comes from the session records of Pi, Devin, DSH and Codex, while OpenCode stays `unknown` because its plugin adds the brief in memory and the store keeps no copy.\n83: \n84: ### The typed attachment block\n85: \n86: `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` reports typed reach twice under `attachedMetrics`:\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 87]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md, lines 79-86\n79: \n80: A line whose locator names no checkout keeps null offer fields and `offerError` `no_checkout`, and the rest of the log is still written with `offerBackfilled: true`.\n81: \n82: `--brief-only` keeps every offer field exactly as the input line holds it, present or absent, and recomputes only `briefDelivered`, because a recorded offer belongs to the head the turn saw and replaying it would describe a different head. Brief delivery now comes from the session records of Pi, Devin, DSH and Codex, while OpenCode stays `unknown` because its plugin adds the brief in memory and the store keeps no copy.\n83: \n84: ### The typed attachment block\n85: \n86: `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` reports typed reach twice under `attachedMetrics`:\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 87]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":8,\"offset\":79,\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794547865607,"end":1794547867188}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794547867200,"sessionID":"ses_e2c9ec714ffefg1SEdXaW10eW8","part":{"partID":"prt_1d3635a74001wZRRElns5AKfDv","sessionID":"ses_e2c9ec714ffefg1SEdXaW10eW8","messageID":"msg_1d36352520014LKUOgIEKJDQMk","type":"tool","id":"call_7cde1f666ca8466a9f6e887b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"cappedOfferRows|leftoverPaths|top three\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"110:| `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Scores `command-prompts.jsonl` under the pinned regime and prints or writes the baseline. Its `attachedMetrics` key holds own-row, attached and combined plain reach per split and per command family, attached false offers, the typed rows where a command and its owner skill read as ambiguous, and the command attached to each row. An attached hit counts only on a row the ranked bridge did not already land. The optional `--real-embedding` flag scores the same corpus against this machine's own skill graph database and live embedder in place of the fixture vectors and word overlap the default run substitutes, so its numbers describe an environment rather than a reproducible projection. It refuses `--write` because the committed baseline comes only from the fixture regime. Before scoring it proves two things, that a live embedder answers and serves the `nomic-embed-text` model family the stored vectors were built with, and that the skill graph database holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. Each row in its `rows` output also carries `offered`, which is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, so it measures reach rather than whether a brief head offered the command. |\n111:| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows either mode to one row and `--json` prints machine-readable output. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `armIncomplete` and `byPolicy`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers on a turn whose brief arrived, `deliveryUnknown` counts rows whose brief state is `unknown`, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n113:| `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"110:| `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Scores `command-prompts.jsonl` under the pinned regime and prints or writes the baseline. Its `attachedMetrics` key holds own-row, attached and combined plain reach per split and per command family, attached false offers, the typed rows where a command and its owner skill read as ambiguous, and the command attached to each row. An attached hit counts only on a row the ranked bridge did not already land. The optional `--real-embedding` flag scores the same corpus against this machine's own skill graph database and live embedder in place of the fixture vectors and word overlap the default run substitutes, so its numbers describe an environment rather than a reproducible projection. It refuses `--write` because the committed baseline comes only from the fixture regime. Before scoring it proves two things, that a live embedder answers and serves the `nomic-embed-text` model family the stored vectors were built with, and that the skill graph database holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. Each row in its `rows` output also carries `offered`, which is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, so it measures reach rather than whether a brief head offered the command. |\n111:| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows either mode to one row and `--json` prints machine-readable output. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `armIncomplete` and `byPolicy`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers on a turn whose brief arrived, `deliveryUnknown` counts rows whose brief state is `unknown`, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n113:| `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"cappedOfferRows|leftoverPaths|top three\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794547866228,"end":1794547867200}}}}
