{"type":"text","timestamp":1794547875042,"sessionID":"ses_e2c9ec714ffefg1SEdXaW10eW8","part":{"id":"prt_1d363748b002155yKxhU1Kv1ZG","sessionID":"ses_e2c9ec714ffefg1SEdXaW10eW8","messageID":"msg_1d36361d6001IWczBqq6B56w5c","type":"text","text":"T032 is complete. The checkbox in `tasks.md` was left unticked.\n\n**File written**\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md` — four edits: the scorer row now lists `offerFieldAbsent`, `cappedOfferRows`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined` and the loop-without-init rule in `unsafe`, plus the Claude `<command-name>` start. The runner row now carries `--brief-only`, the `codex-hooks-unapproved` refusal and the HEAD restore with `leftoverPaths`. The backfill section explains what `--brief-only` preserves and which runtimes answer delivery. The capture row explains the row-level `offered` flag.\n\n**Verify output**\n\n```\n--- offerUnknown (expect no output) ---\nexit=1\n--- distinct tokens (expect 10) ---\n      10\n```\n\nMatches the task's expectation: `offerUnknown` prints nothing, and the alternation yields exactly 10 distinct tokens.\n\n`git status` for that path lists only the README as modified. Nothing was blocked, and I could not tick the checkbox by instruction.","time":{"start":1794547872907,"end":1794547875042}}}
